            <ArticleTitle>Partial annular pancreas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>402-403</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Annular pancreas is a developmental anomaly that can be associated with other conditions such as Down syndrome, duodenal atresia, and Hirschsprung disease. A band of pancreatic tissue, in continuity with the pancreatic head, completely or incompletely encircles the descending duodenum, sometimes assuming a &quot;crocodile jaw&quot; configuration. We present the case of an adult who presented with epigastric pain and vomiting and was found to have annular pancreas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
